# Centre and smooth directional Board rotation

Rotate the complete Board around its own geometric centre and animate each action through the requested 90-degree direction without wraparound artifacts.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The rotation pivot is the geometric centre of the rendered Board, derived from Board geometry rather than the containing screen rectangle.
- [x] Overview bias, safe-area space, fixed controls, and bottom-bar space do not displace the Board's rotation pivot.
- [x] Rotate-left animates exactly 90 degrees counter-clockwise, including the first left action from the default orientation.
- [x] Rotate-right animates exactly 90 degrees clockwise.
- [x] A transition across the persisted orientation wrap point never takes the visually longer 270-degree route.
- [x] Rotation uses smooth acceleration and deceleration without an abrupt start or stop.
- [x] Repeated taps resolve deterministically without accumulating geometric drift or leaving an intermediate visual orientation.
- [x] Four completed turns in either direction return to the original presentation.
- [x] Terrain, numbers, roads, buildings, ghosts, and applicable interaction targets share the same pivot and animation.
- [x] Logical Board coordinates remain unchanged and the final quarter-turn orientation continues to persist with the active game.
- [x] Relaunching restores the persisted final orientation without replaying an animation.
- [x] Existing Overview/Detail scale, Detail panning, tap-to-focus, and view-mode hit testing remain correct at every orientation.
- [x] SCR-001 is updated with the geometric-centre and directional-animation behavior before implementation is completed.
- [x] Geometry, state-transition, and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused animation, rapid-tap, relaunch, and rotated-gesture checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- Use a presentation angle or equivalent transition state that can preserve direction independently of the normalized persisted quarter-turn value.
- Continuous free rotation is out of scope.

## Evidence

- Added an unbounded presentation-quarter-turn state initialized from the normalized persisted orientation, so each left/right tap advances exactly −90/+90 degrees across wrap points.
- Applied a zero-bounce 0.42-second smooth animation while continuing to persist only the normalized orientation.
- Derived the rotation anchor from the bounding centre of the rendered hex vertices at the current scale and viewport origin.
- Added unit coverage for initial-left, west-to-north right wrap, four-turn direction, and standard Board geometric-centre calculation.
- Updated SCR-001 with the pivot and animation contract.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
